    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 50 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic and reworked everything that keys off the household. Changes in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. **`householdIdFor(lastName, postcode)`** \u2014 now derives the household id as the **first 12 hex characters of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`** (using the existing `collapse()` for the normalized last name), replacing the old 16-char hash over `(lastName, address)`. Owners with the same last name and postcode now share it automatically.\n\n2. **`addOwner`** \u2014 computes the household id from `owner.getPostcode()` instead of the address, and stores it (so `householdMemberCount`, computed via `countHouseholdMembers` keyed on that id, and duplicate detection all use the computed value).\n\n3. **`rejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 compares against each existing owner's `householdIdFor(lastName, postcode)`. Since a matching household now means the record already exists, a second owner with the same lastName+postcode is rejected as a **409 household duplicate**, unless `sharesHousehold` is set, which only bypasses that block (it no longer creates the link \u2014 the link is computed).\n\n4. **`findPossibleDuplicateOf`** \u2014 returns `null` when `sharesHousehold` is set: a declared household member is created and is **not** flagged as a possible duplicate. (The soft-match key was exactly `(lastName, postcode)` = the household key, so a co-member reached here can only be a declared one.)\n\nSupporting doc/message updates in `DuplicateHouseholdException` and `ExceptionControllerAdvice` now describe the `(lastName, postcode)` key and name `postcode` (rather than `address`) in the 409 `errors` array.\n\nThe behavior now matches the spec and all household tests (Cp10 reject, Cp11/Cp36 shared id, Cp23 household-size membership level, Cp28 identity collision, Cp35 declared-member-not-flagged) plus the unchanged identity tests (Cp03, Cp13, Cp15, Cp24, Cp25).",
